I renamed the original `pay` body to a private `recordPayment` and made `pay` a thin wrapper around it. If the reference matches an earlier non-empty one (compared case-insensitively with `toLowerCase`, with no trimming or accent folding), the wrapper runs the original on a copy of the payments list, so any existing throw still happens. It then puts the original list back and returns 0. Otherwise it calls the original unchanged.

I couldn't see the body of `pay`, so I didn't edit inside it. If it changes anything other than `this.payments`, a refused duplicate would leave that change behind. If you paste the body, I can put the check inside it instead.
